  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A ball of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is dropped from a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> on a platform fixed at the top of a vertical spring (as shown in figure). The ball stays on the platform and the platform is depressed by a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. The spring constant is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />(Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/770eafa4-cf51-4b4b-9514-2b1c8d8c9864-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 231px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "120",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/edf8848b-dc71-4b91-beba-68ad086e439d-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 219px;\" /></p><p>Loss in the gravitational potential energy of the ball= gain in the potential energy by the spring</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>gravitational</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>spring</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
